---
title: The company page
description: The header, the summary and each tab of a company page, and how to change a company's details, GST settings, bank accounts and KYC.
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

Select a company in the list to open its page. The top shows the name, whether it is a **Client** or a **Related entity**, the UEN, industry and jurisdiction, and the ACRA status when it needs attention. The buttons at the top right are **New opportunity** (for users with the CRM suite; see [CRM](/en/crm/opportunities/)) and, for managers, **End service for this client** (see [End or restore service](/en/clients/end-service/)).

If ACRA shows the company as struck off or otherwise ended while your firm still serves it, a banner says so, with the date of the ACRA data.

**Contact summary** under the header shows the client's outstanding and overdue **Invoices** and its **Work Items** (cases in progress, waiting, blocked and overdue). Select **Hide summary** to fold it.

## The tabs

| Tab | Contents |
|---|---|
| **Details** | The company's details, contact details, accounting dates, GST, bank accounts, access, client team and compliance (below). |
| **Timeline** | Notes, cases and documents of the company in date order. Write a note in the box and select **Post**; type @ to notify a colleague. Filter with **All**, **Notes**, **Cases** and **Documents**. |
| **Activity** | Every change to the company's details: the field, the change, who made it and when. |
| **Cases** | The company's cases, grouped as open, done and closed. **Start a Case** starts a new one for this company (see [Workspaces and cases](/en/getting-started/workspaces-cases/#start-a-case)). |
| **Time & Budget** | Not in use yet: time and budget are not tracked. |
| **Relationships** | Directors, shareholders, secretaries, contact persons and related companies. See [Relationships](/en/clients/relationships/). |
| **Services** | The services from the client's signed contracts, with the agreed price and delivery. **Start a case** starts a case for a service. |
| **Invoices** | The client's invoices, the amounts outstanding and overdue, **+ New invoice**, and **Payment reminders for this client** to turn reminders on or off. See [Invoices](/en/invoices/overview/). |
| **Books** | The client's books, read-only. Shown to users with the Tax suite. To change the books, start a bookkeeping case (see [Bookkeeping workbench](/en/bookkeeping/getting-started/)). |

Some tabs may be missing if the company is limited to an access list and you are not on it (see [Who can see a company](/en/clients/access/)).

## Change the company's details

On **Details**, select a field, change it and press Enter or select outside it; each field is saved on its own. The sections are:

| Section | Contents |
|---|---|
| **Basics** | Name, UEN, incorporation date, industry, **Language** (the language for the client's documents and messages), **Contact Type** (for example Direct End-client, Vendor or Holding Company of Client) and **Tags**. |
| **Contact details** | Address, e-mail, phone, mobile, website and a SharePoint link. **Fill address from postal code** looks up a Singapore postal code; check the address and select **Save this address**. |
| **Accounting details** | **Financial Year End** and **Jurisdiction**. **Next AGM Due** (FYE + 6 months) and **Next AR Due** (FYE + 7 months) are worked out from the FYE and do not include extensions granted by ACRA. **Last AGM Date** and **Last AR Filed** are filled in by the annual return case. |
| **GST** | See below. |
| **Bank accounts** | See below. |
| **Access** | Who can see the company. See [Who can see a company](/en/clients/access/). |

On the right:

- **Client team** — **Assigned to** (changed by managers), and the people in charge of the client: director, manager, person, accountant, secretary in charge, and Corppass admin.
- **Compliance** — the KYC status, the **ACRA company status** with its date, and the SSIC codes. **Edit SSIC & KYC** changes the SSIC codes and the jurisdiction; managers can also set the **KYC conclusion**: the status (Not started, Passed, Failed or Expired), the date it was decided, the expiry date and the KYC report.

### GST

The **GST** section shows whether the company is registered. Select **Edit GST settings** to set **GST Company**, **GST No.**, **GST Effective From**, **GST Deregistered On**, **GST Filing Frequency** (Quarterly or Monthly) and **GST Quarter Cycle**, then **Save GST settings**. **GST Settings Set By** shows whether a person or the AI bookkeeping run set them.

The **IRAS GST register** panel compares the GST number with the IRAS register and warns of differences. Select **Check with IRAS now** to check it at once; otherwise it is checked again automatically. The check never changes your settings.

### Bank accounts

The register of the company's bank accounts and company credit cards, used by the books. Select **Add bank account**, fill in the type, currency, bank, label, account number and the date it was opened, and select **Add to register**. Account numbers are shown masked. Use **Edit** to correct an account, **Close account** when it is closed, and **Link to the books** to connect it to the bookkeeping.
